\}=7\\,⟹\\,{max}_{‖x‖=1}\\{‖Ax‖\\}=\\sqrt{7}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the semi-major axis of our ellipse is $\\sqrt{7}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269230 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "862d7336-1d68-5324-8a48-626b5ab3fe1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267328} {:answer/id #uuid "ace6192e-8c33-5978-a97c-18fb7456a6e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267704} {:answer/id #uuid "c9cc3d50-c939-57bb-abf8-9b83ef1957ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267955} {:answer/id #uuid "ce9a5c87-ce40-5fa9-a431-5e8054488051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267991} {:answer/id #uuid "edd6cf5d-5e7b-5bae-ba67-eac4418c2dcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267955} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c64cec0-1f04-5d87-8e4d-1ea5c1b48553" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268451}] :question/id #uuid "e48008ac-4acd-5d33-8b94-d523fa814086" :question/math-academy-id "q-139492" :question/problem "A $2\\times 3$ matrix $A$ maps the unit sphere $\\{x\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}$ from ${R}^{3}$ onto an ellipse in ${R}^{2}.$ Given that the eigenvalues of ${A}^{T}A$ are $12,$ $9,$ and $0,$ find the length of the ellipse's semi-major axis." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ maps the unit sphere $\\{x\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}$ from ${R}^{3}$ onto the ellipse $\\{Ax\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}$ in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nFirst, let's re-write the squared distance from the origin to the point $Ax$ on our ellipse, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖Ax{‖}^{2} & =(Ax)^{T}(Ax) \\\\  & =({x}^{T}\\,{A}^{T})(Ax) \\\\  & ={x}^{T}\\,({A}^{T}\\,A)x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere ${x}^{T}({A}^{T}A)x$ is the quadratic form with the matrix ${A}^{T}A.$ \n\nThe maximum value of this quadratic form, when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of the matrix ${A}^{T}A.$\n\nSince the largest eigenvalue of ${A}^{T}A$ is $12,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{max}_{‖x‖=1}\\{‖Ax{‖}^{2}\\}=12\\,⟹\\,{max}_{‖x‖=1}\\{‖Ax‖\\}=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the semi-major axis of our ellipse is $2\\sqrt{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269236 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e0290b-b214-51b9-ae5b-fc3e291433d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266285} {:answer/id #uuid "4d569cb3-e268-51d7-8e1f-47a0e048ffa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266830} {:answer/id #uuid "50423a6e-7974-582d-a76f-cac676cf369c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266858} {:answer/id #uuid "67f7f843-8d99-5b2c-a258-bfa87e57387b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267065} {:answer/id #uuid "bccbe989-ecf7-53c3-8c04-5337fd9a0320" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266858} :answer-field/id #uuid "a82d9035-63ea-54b8-90da-3fbf50bd2ad3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268705}] :question/id #uuid "72c2ac9a-8e8a-51d7-84bb-f51632a65f59" :question/math-academy-id "q-139526" :question/problem "A $2\\times 3$ matrix $A$ maps the unit sphere $\\{x\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}$ from ${R}^{3}$ onto an ellipse in ${R}^{2}.$ Given that the eigenvalues of ${A}^{T}A$ are $15,$ $10,$ and $0,$ find the length of the ellipse's semi-major axis." :question/worked-solution "The mat