40 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308634 :question/id #uuid "691520cf-4380-50be-8b5c-ac8a181c7472"} :step/id #uuid "711a72fe-d404-510a-8960-ed2ab6a98eaa"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558662 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558553 :question/id #uuid "a83f3a56-7f37-59d6-8ed6-dd0cc81608ee"} :step/id #uuid "9b0e4e07-3c1a-5e15-8966-efc4693d635c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558595}}] :activity/title "Fundamental Matrices" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557860}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050228 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221420 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221191 :question/id #uuid "4874a486-2cf1-5b6e-ae4f-52579f03b077" :question/math-academy-id "e-21695" :question/problem "![](images/28/28eeada9d539377f372fd73155f08215e6a0eb3b3503b88e05c85e38977c024a.svg)\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions $\\mathbf x_1$ and $\\mathbf x_2,$ shown above. Find the fundamental matrix for the system." :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system $\\mathbf{x}' = A \\mathbf{x},$ where $A$ is an $n \\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $\\Phi(t)$ of the system is an $n \\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our cases, we have a $2 \\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}=\\begin{bmatrix}4{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}4t \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}=\\begin{bmatrix}4t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 4{e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n![](images/89/892921f10f5b3db34b140a6d7608bdb4771fd1ad055319e7ff5d4edceb527d3a.svg)\n\n**Note:** The columns of $\\Phi$ can be written in any order."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "af871f3d-da9e-5fd3-a61f-94e155ccf2b3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0388fd29-b8b2-576b-a6c9-9265590bee1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442485} {:answer/id #uuid "135f6c78-b365-50be-89db-444d4d16ab70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{-2t} & -{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442489} {:answer/id #uuid "3c74cfd1-a038-5c50-bfb1-5cecb7ed1534" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{-2} & -{e}^{2} \\\\ {e}^{-2} & {e}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442501} {:answer/id #uuid "bb791218-a743-55a3-afe5-6608ffd45328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442524} {:answer/id #uuid "feb3ec21-6632-5781-b732-b19423bbbfa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{-2t} & 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{-2t} & 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442536} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bff80bf-991a-5e44-9565-955b85bdc117" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220547}] :question/id #uuid "f190e3a4-5efc-5caa-a01f-c8d68875b312" :question/math-academy-id "q-333701" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our cases, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}=\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}=\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{-2t} & 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ {e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221999 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8768dd56-c0fc-583e-822c-6575903b9078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220667} {:answer/id #uuid "89daedea-da9e-59f9-ad22-509d3847c15f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}e^{t}\\cos 2t & -e^{t}\\sin 2t \\\\ e^{t}\\sin 2t & e^{t}\\cos 2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220668} {:answer/id #uuid "d66f2830-46a6-5121-889a-63b107df6397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos 2t & -\\sin 2t \\\\ \\sin 2t & \\cos 2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220669} {:answer/id #uuid "5ed2e693-a120-58c3-95fc-d17cb9ff7c55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}e^{t}\\cos t & e^{t}\\sin t \\\\ -e^{t}\\sin t & e^{t}\\cos t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220670} {:answer/id #uuid "7aebd347-1fac-5f4a-88d1-5def198f349e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}e\\cos 2 & -e\\sin 2 \\\\ e\\sin 2 & e\\cos 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220671}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7634ac73-0ede-5218-abe9-859f177734ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220666} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3b3ad7c-a785-5d6b-b99f-8f4de368554c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}e\\operatorname{cos}⁡2 & -e\\operatorname{sin}⁡2 \\\\ e\\operatorname{sin}⁡2 & e\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398789} {:answer/id #uuid "db600daa-372c-5b3f-a72d-c8846aa238fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398790} {:answer/id #uuid "b571b8b5-c9f1-50e2-a6c6-b293be65a40b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ -{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398791} {:answer/id #uuid "6c266f0b-bbf3-576d-8645-acb043be2282" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398792} {:answer/id #uuid "e03700f3-0e96-509e-b9e8-a17953714bc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398792} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ab06ed4-7b45-5ef0-9d7c-02e4dbb72cb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398788}] :question/id #uuid "ecd4b4f8-b1ae-5164-9bed-1e7df536d7e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-334329" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}=\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1edb8b15-9c42-5ca3-83c4-d929582f111c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2t \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305446} {:answer/id #uuid "27f7325e-9947-5c17-9571-b7d83bfa32f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{3t} & 2t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305528} {:answer/id #uuid "4254f203-f627-577b-8657-34e13674c937" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{3t} & 0 \\\\ 2t{e}^{3t} & 2{e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305807} {:answer/id #uuid "61fdfda5-f3c4-5bc3-90cd-a5e62591a6c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306100} {:answer/id #uuid "621d2f22-209e-5423-9f78-9f2cd284fc99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{3} & 2{e}^{3} \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{3t} & 2t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305528} :answer-field/id #uuid "895f7ab0-7fbf-53a6-b46d-5f2832b8b575" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307953}] :question/id #uuid "0a96ede4-5f22-51e8-acbb-7d3f2a89ee5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-334327" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2t \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}=\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2t \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}=\\begin{bmatrix}2t{e}^{3t} \\\\ -{e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{3t} & 2t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308600 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c9dce11-9930-5ed8-a98a-71b2c6d613f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & {e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305731} {:answer/id #uuid "457fdc35-522e-54bf-b4a2-96a44738c939" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305834} {:answer/id #uuid "6a690293-bc00-5f55-add0-38bfbd8cd231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306167} {:answer/id #uuid "d0722a55-c81c-5911-86e0-d5540fd6d7a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2 & -{e}^{-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2 \\\\ {e}^{-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2 & {e}^{-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307079} {:answer/id #uuid "d321f46a-76a7-5be1-b689-e83b8deece3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}\\operatorn