t} :answer/value "factoring out $A$ on the left" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391276} {:answer/id #uuid "63c0991b-ad6e-5f6a-98b8-643da1aae492" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "transposing the matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391277} {:answer/id #uuid "351118ef-d9b7-5b2c-8103-6248dbbc0401" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating again" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391278} {:answer/id #uuid "cafa980d-badb-57fc-a8c3-a2ffc2a64bf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ(t)$ to both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "factoring out $A$ on the left" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391276} :answer-field/id #uuid "155738af-3e2a-57a9-a635-a3db6456eb1e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391275}] :question/id #uuid "49e5968a-1ea4-5510-81b8-9a383e60e6d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-333719" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A\\,Φ(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $[a,\\,b]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $a$ and $b.$*\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L4}$ and substitution from lines {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent solutions of the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ This means that each column satisfies the differential equation. In particular, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that ${x}_{1}\\text{ is a solution of the system}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L4}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ By definition, the derivative of $Φ(t)$ is obtained by differentiating each column,\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}^{′}(t) & {x}_{2}^{′}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ and ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$ from $\\text{L3},$ we substitute each derivative into the matrix to get\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\,| & | \\\\ A{x}_{1}(t) & A{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substitution from $\\text{L2}\\text{ and }\\text{L3}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ We now factor the matrix $A$ on the left:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\,| & | \\\\ A{x}_{1}(t) & A{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{bmatrix}=A\\begin{bmatrix}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{bmatrix}=AΦ(t)\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{factoring out }A\\text{ on the left}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396895 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5852157-70f8-5e93-89b0-59d8b774ff3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396897} {:answer/id #uuid "990ecc42-c4e6-5578-a0da-d91b13097a44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding the vectors ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396898} {:answer/id #uuid "7722083e-e7dc-572c-9e33-46131eb0f8b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying $Φ(t)$ with it's inverse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396899} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d2992c-33d6-5911-8f6b-9bda3e200baa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396900} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3682025-d096-56bd-bf59-0048dee77ced" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396896} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea29c33a-1099-547c-826a-fd0e927691bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Φ}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396902} {:answer/id #uuid "eda2dd9e-6754-5d8c-bfd6-9ae76f866cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396903} {:answer/id #uuid "5c373e55-b761-5339-b7ae-18f49f46ac45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396904} {:answer/id #uuid "f31c325d-17cf-5219-a1cb-6658f11fd045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Φ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Φ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396905} :answer-field/id #uuid "eedfdc9d-7a1b-5144-98ef-079b39f1a6cd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396901} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42514761-6af9-5f0a-acd2-e9be42e06afe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396907} {:answer/id #uuid "7caef4bf-95b8-571b-aaa3-5210003d59f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of diagonalizable matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396908} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7d92b1-be8e-5617-880a-12beb90f314b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396909} {:answer/id #uuid "47b36cde-80ca-5b95-9fb8-d497515c1778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396909} :answer-field/id #uuid "25b2d3de-e14d-5e49-b765-fcc7eb25aafa" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396906} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "452a40cb-853e-5f67-a98a-fbeeccb65acb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first row" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396912} {:answer/id #uuid "a4c30172-18f7-52e1-95bc-79d14f8a4bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "diagonals" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396913} {:answer/id #uuid "c2045390-0f53-5f3d-8afa-92c13462bafa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "columns" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396914} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a29805-59cc-5557-a9b9-6313452c9c94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "rows" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "columns" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396914} :answer-field/id #uuid "c98b9a18-7c6a-59cb-8ce5-cb6ffe8a471b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396911}] :question/id #uuid "accc1e17-f130-5583-b331-4d6a4ed72254" :question/math-academy-id "q-336106" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that every solution $x(t)$ can be written in the form $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c=[{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}]^{T}$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of solutions\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)$ can be written as $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)\\,c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ introduces the notation for the {{field-1}} of {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first interpret line $\\text{L1}.$ Line $\\text{L1}$ introduces the notation for the $\\text{columns}$ of $Φ,$ namely the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ These functions are the fundamental solutions of the system.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Once ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis, every solution $x(t)$ of the system can be expressed uniquely as a linear combination\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{the definition of a basis}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c886e4d-ec71-526e-9fca-44411eb71087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396918} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee05532-dfb9-529e-b73c-929366f56b5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396919} {:answer/id #uuid "1c690c80-9317-5e41-aaae-07f5c0248385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396920} {:answer/id #uuid "da083ae6-571f-54bb-bc13-27bab5c4d1b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396920} :answer-field/id #uuid "319112f1-c5cd-5b59-bc98-0fbaa63699a8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396917} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f41205b8-acc0-5664-955b-74b059485116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396923} {:answer/id #uuid "82374921-7bf9-535e-9301-cd8fcd3d1de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the properties of determinants" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396924} {:answer/id #uuid "6e8e658e-f066-597f-abf6-933f8b8713c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property of equality" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396925} {:answer/id #uuid "1a09ff54-d141-5e15-a5d8-b2bb7e05d498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property of equality" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396925} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c455c64-6a5a-53e9-8592-0cd96bbb254d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396922} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3dfad07-3750-584e-9f6f-d30755695967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396928} {:answer/id #uuid "995b3536-4529-5769-9f9a-f34c8177e004" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying $Φ(t)$ with it's inverse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396929} {:answer/id #uuid "dd384e88-52b2-55f6-8382-7ee54663a081" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396930} {:answer/id #uuid "83c3e129-5f38-5e53-b0a2-61bbd06b2d41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396931} :answer-field/id #uuid "f108e315-8611-579e-a41e-01f211239093" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396927} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "638ac533-2df7-530f-9f02-d6db96ca8dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396933} {:answer/id #uuid "fe02d4db-11ef-5015-aea5-bf6b6e4b9f87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396934} {:answer/id #uuid "1a1b6e19-58ed-5e2e-97f8-48746da9e753" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396933} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe7c7b3b-bbe4-57bb-8ae1-e9580b65ffd9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396932}] :question/id #uuid "9fcd6208-dde9-5e8a-b2c1-ff9f0dade0db" :question/math-academy-id "q-336107" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that every solution $x(t)$ can be written in the form $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c=[{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}]^{T}$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of solutions\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)$ can be written as $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)\\,c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from {{field-1}} by the definition of a fundamental matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-3}} by {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the definition of a fundamental matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are the columns of $Φ(t),$ we can write\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThen by the definition of matrix multiplication,\n\n$$\nΦ(t)\\,c=\\begin{bmatrix}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of matrix multiplication}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ In $\\text{L3}$ we have $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t),$ and in $\\text{L4}$ we have $Φ(t)c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).$ Since both expressions are equal to the same quantity, the transitive property of equality gives $x(t)=Φ(t)c.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L3 and L4}$ by the $\\text{the transitive property of equality}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442561 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01bc519d-9d8a-5a50-9ddd-0576fdcea192" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is diagonalizable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442483} {:answer/id #uuid "4fee71ee-9bfc-53d1-9720-277b632cbc77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442506} {:answer/id #uuid "99dac2c2-2f9a-5177-aec9-2c19611bdcf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating each column" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442519} {:answer/id #uuid "e802edfb-19c6-540a-a7d5-687f645229b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442531} :answer-field/id #uuid "2028cfb9-9d36-500c-b53c-d5c401100c51" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ad643c3-58b8-599d-80d5-1120b49cec66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442500} {:answer/id #uuid "97e4fa85-19f4-5d72-a2e5-d206dea9dd14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442518} {:answer/id #uuid "c1306f31-3a02-5b1e-8df0-d8052ca6d7e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442527} {:answer/id #uuid "fed7e9c9-709f-5270-9ace-aa401742d738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442518} :answer-field/id #uuid "95dff24a-69a1-5c42-aa00-bca2089747a2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442548} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02322a89-1398-5bad-8e30-a0a0a268214d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "transposing the matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442484} {:answer/id #uuid "14fbbddb-48b0-5865-92fb-6528fd13c65e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by $A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442490} {:answer/id #uuid "afe05a9e-d5c2-5aa1-9814-2d2e80429809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating each column" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442522} {:answer/id #uuid "d4336788-b670-5b22-9efc-4971c7505f31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ(t)$ to both sides" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating each column" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442522} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8ae518a-9958-5b32-a5fd-7a9d3da57763" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442554}] :question/id #uuid "df1d5701-ba5a-54b3-9982-7187c6baef60" :question/math-academy-id "q-336312" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A\\,Φ(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $[a,\\,b]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $a$ and $b.$*\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix and line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ and substitution from line {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)],$ the derivative of $Φ(t)$ is obtained by differentiating each column:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)].\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating each column}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its \ncolumns are linearly independent solutions of the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ Line $\\text{L1}$ identifies ${x}_{1}(t)$ as a column of $Φ(t),$ so ${x}_{1}(t)$ must satisfy the differential equation. In particular,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix and $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ From $\\text{L6}$ we have ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)].$ Using $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$ from $\\text{L1},$ we substitute to obtain ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t).$ Thus, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by substitution from $\\text{L1}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498522 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09d0162a-0c31-57bd-bb88-fdfa4dc8e68e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "columns" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497822} {:answer/id #uuid "5f91266e-571d-5556-9e28-0c64ca72bbde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "diagonals" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498025} {:answer/id #uuid "ce4ccd02-457b-505d-be66-2a3ce1983dc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first row" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498265} {:answer/id #uuid "e0717cf0-2277-5799-aeb4-bd7df48e84fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "rows" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "columns" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497822} :answer-field/id #uuid "691f6c70-3e94-5cde-bb06-839111864eb1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498407} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4909c353-7e8a-5cb8-b25e-ad22a33b46c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of diagonalizable matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497966} {:answer/id #uuid "4a9b9084-c9c1-58b5-a890-2458f7916ba6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497970} {:answer/id #uuid "aca1d897-83fa-5953-b387-6aa8cac56164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498183} {:answer/id #uuid "d0d5cf45-87b2-58ae-b6b6-07a8c858f7b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498183} :answer-field/id #uuid "78b2f140-f551-5793-a29c-4fb476575aec" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498419} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37508ceb-d284-5a06-b3ec-936f412805af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497922} {:answer/id 