ible for all $t$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ introduces the notation for the {{field-1}} of {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line {{field-4}} by the properties of invertible matrices." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first interpret line $\\text{L1}.$ Line $\\text{L1}$ introduces the notation for the $\\text{columns}$ of $Φ,$ namely the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ These functions are the fundamental solutions of the system.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Recall that a square matrix is invertible when its determinant is nonzero. Since in $\\text{L3}$ we have that $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t,$ it follows that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t.$ Thus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by the properties of invertible matrices."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498584 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bd46542-9a80-5921-aec9-c4e0eab15d02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497935} {:answer/id #uuid "4a0c74f4-d2e2-5a08-a0ec-15c44fc1a4f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497968} {:answer/id #uuid "9789113b-b31f-54b4-b8fe-4662096868cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498144} {:answer/id #uuid "d57a43c8-dd84-5c2d-96ed-8415ae761576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498277}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497968} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b347ff5-a360-5553-944a-1fd66d4ece0a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498386} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64196c4e-29d7-5962-b257-222a15c4588d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498039} {:answer/id #uuid "ce4515ff-f000-5d07-9351-f9cf05460b2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498264} {:answer/id #uuid "cf0b0954-c00e-51da-a8ca-5afe64dfb0ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498269} {:answer/id #uuid "efe24b44-977f-576a-b20f-de491d1bb43f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying $Φ(t)$ with its inverse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498264} :answer-field/id #uuid "69513af4-694f-5ca8-996c-0c33d8fa859d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498408} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c1b43a8-0bad-584d-8658-946b10a53deb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497825} {:answer/id #uuid "f03bcfca-1c79-5dcc-a769-287b903a87de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498327} {:answer/id #uuid "fd2fe107-c83d-541c-ad1f-d9f4feb898de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying $Φ(t)$ with its inverse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498353} {:answer/id #uuid "fd8a0c7f-af95-54f9-89f1-fb7222915fbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498327} :answer-field/id #uuid "84273087-2e18-501d-872d-5ad466c8d262" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498424}] :question/id #uuid "d656b9e3-27c9-51a6-a70f-c9d56643be83" :question/math-academy-id "q-336108" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that every solution $x(t)$ can be written in the form $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c=[{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}]^{T}$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of solutions\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)$ can be written as $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)\\,c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-3}} by the transitive property of equality." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Once ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis, every solution $x(t)$ of the system can be expressed uniquely as a linear combination\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{the definition of a basis}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are the columns of $Φ(t),$ we can write\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThen by the definition of matrix multiplication,\n\n$$\nΦ(t)\\,c=\\begin{bmatrix}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of matrix multiplication}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ In $\\text{L3}$ we have $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t),$ and in $\\text{L4}$ we have $Φ(t)c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).$ Since both expressions are equal to the same quantity, the transitive property of equality gives $x(t)=Φ(t)c.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L3 and L4}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533984 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21f04a48-e3d9-5285-9be6-a47bfb7a3162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533221} {:answer/id #uuid "806ffe8b-ec3d-5752-b9c6-7e479c231b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533443} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7ddf96-482e-5261-9f56-9cabb5f0cd3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533600} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ac113d-a092-55a0-828c-3cce578364b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533443} :answer-field/id #uuid "047d2299-ba3b-5217-bd76-392b196edadf" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533773} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "175e98b0-2179-5c38-aec4-02ea135fddfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Φ}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533192} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb78a1e-acbc-582f-9896-4a25b60643c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Φ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533330} {:answer/id #uuid "85fcf6d7-1b0b-5bf0-afee-87974db835f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533455} {:answer/id #uuid "ce4797d8-fe35-5b5b-b08e-1c83d6082952" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Φ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533330} :answer-field/id #uuid "20fff794-00dd-50a8-9256-5d3d679c4c80" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fa5012c-8bff-5182-bdc1-c3192d2fa42b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of diagonalizable matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533179} {:answer/id #uuid "c9a4e473-005c-5bad-b050-c349b4619ab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533622} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe5eb6f-4d7a-5247-87cc-a29690e1564d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533644} {:answer/id #uuid "e959566f-e723-58b3-9ab2-a51a923ed3cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533714} :answer-field/id #uuid "99e500e9-2419-5436-86f7-bd0983f12961" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533896} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a59e584-278d-59db-b6ea-7b7977de0f71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "columns" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533159} {:answer/id #uuid "79c8042c-d474-5943-aed4-1c689601cb7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "diagonals" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533428} {:answer/id #uuid "b483bb15-790a-5e86-a64e-5ba317eecac7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first row" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533578} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4405cf-0772-5f28-9f99-4a05e4a8fb85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "rows" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "columns" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533159} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8b3efd3-b7c3-58e8-b4b9-9e7263c863ee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533964}] :question/id #uuid "20281150-3bf1-5302-a5be-765695a3b8d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-336094" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ introduces the notation for the {{field-1}} of {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from line {{field-4}} by the properties of determinants." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first interpret line $\\text{L1}.$ Line $\\text{L1}$ introduces the notation for the $\\text{columns}$ of $Φ,$ namely the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ These functions are the fundamental solutions of the system.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Recall that a matrix has linearly independent columns if and only if its determinant is nonzero. Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for any particular $t,$\n\n$$\ndet(Φ(t))\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by the properties of determinants."}] :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221422 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221192 :question/id #uuid "3e053d6d-f051-5c4c-a20b-1e90b2d5941b" :question/math-academy-id "e-21696" :question/problem "![](images/23/23c904878889e799744f2f4df095727d82a26050d15a01e0df06be6e3838b48d.svg)\nConsider the system of linear ODEs $\\mathbf{x}' = A\\mathbf{x}$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix $\\Phi(t)$ for this system." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\mathbf x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system $\\mathbf x'(t) = A\\mathbf x(t),$ denoted $\\Phi_0(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n\\Phi_0'(t) = A\\Phi_0(t), \\quad \\Phi_0(0)  = I_n,\n$$\n\nwhere $I_n$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{0} & -7{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 7{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_0$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda) = \\alpha_1 \\lambda + \\alpha_0.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1 = 7\\textrm{i}t, \\qquad\n\\lambda_2 = -7\\textrm{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((7\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(7\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(7\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+7\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_0{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) \\\\ 7{\\alpha }_{1}t &=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{7t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_0$ into the expressions for the required entries of $e^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) \\\\ 7{\\alpha }_{1}t & =7\\cdot \\frac{1}{7t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n![](images/74/744b1de9acba2740bac7ebc54d79fb7ae82e98cb0576492f4d9503bb0b2a71a8.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66c99cda-25a5-50f2-903b-bfb1fdc5fa10" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221988 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4475a7f4-c95c-5c55-8109-0e9ea886a2a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545329} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa786690-2dc1-59f3-a44d-639db8237f3d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10f335ea-9d53-5bd8-a277-0e71096d1701" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545230} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee77c4e2-6eb2-5db9-8618-4ba0d57d6223" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220584} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4192bd6-a9b5-5e3c-a850-538acc11b68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545587} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f7022e0-ee16-5d5b-b4f3-9eb2d8be983b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220585} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "227c788b-a841-56fc-9c67-21ee4721d3f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "te^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "te^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545272} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c1b35ed-a68f-5e20-b0c8-7a1d98ca67ae" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220586}] :question/id #uuid "d2008090-84f9-50fd-9af0-82b54be4b43f" :question/math-academy-id "q-333712" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & {\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 0 & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=2t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}r(2t)={e}^{2t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(2t)={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{2t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n2t{e}^{2t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}(1-2t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =2{e}^{2t}t+{e}^{2t}(1-2t) \\\\  & ={e}^{2t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & ={e}^{2t}t \\\\  & =t{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06b62f64-a72a-58c3-83b7-f04a2c64a243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305212} {:answer/id #uuid "1727af84-c111-5aa6-af98-970d01d617df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442492} :answer-field/id #uuid "38ab63d4-df22-5b52-9665-41a9dd7da8dd" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29616b45-1873-5c52-bde7-ea7fad263666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305540} {:answer/id #uuid "18f3666c-fa87-56a3-a25f-71b0d5b23487" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442493} :answer-field/id #uuid "39f8022a-afa7-5402-9578-ce5abfc3468c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307701} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1d6721b-ff98-5c3e-ad88-04c1ddec1e8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307378} {:answer/id #uuid "caa9d9cb-c73f-5b34-8a78-86a7733240c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442528} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c6472ca-2c4e-5da6-9f5a-4788af95a430" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307871} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94eeb383-7b17-545d-8da7-02f82d01ed4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306553} {:answer/id #uuid "62e44a13-82dc-5b4c-af8f-b45690546571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442511} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2155b73-1362-5f64-bf35-7930dcaeeb4a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308289}] :question/id #uuid "5ca7cf8a-29b9-5dc9-9eb7-2eb98441be57" :question/math-academy-id "q-333713" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -2{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=2\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((2\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(2\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(2\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+2\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t &=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308497 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2ca6901-556b-5960-a3bd-8d0552587579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}-{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}-{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307252} :answer-field/id #uuid "09352193-2085-5ed0-9dac-3b45c1b2f367" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307553} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2961f6c2-30e1-5479-98d1-86e05fd1e48e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}-{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}-{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305541} :answer-field/id #uuid "743ad797-c4e6-5a90-81e7-9503d1668174" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307887}] :question/id #uuid "eff0b088-3db3-5966-a1d7-4ea54d40635c" :question/math-academy-id "q-333715" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$ |  | ${e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t}$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | ${e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t}$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-2t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2t,\n$$\n\nboth of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-2t) &={e}^{-2t} \\\\ r(2t) &={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{-2t} \\\\ 2t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtraction the second equation from the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-4t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-2t}-{e}^{2t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{4t}({e}^{-2t}-{e}^{2t}).\n$$\n\n- Adding the first and the second equations, we get\n\n$$\n2{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-2t}+{e}^{2t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-2t}+{e}^{2t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-2t}+{e}^{2t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t}) \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4t}({e}^{-4t}-{e}^{4t}))t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2t}-{e}^{-2t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}-{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}-{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308609 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d8223f6-d576-5e04-89fc-1464abef50dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306050} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cae7130-92fe-567b-b98b-6f508a21ed99" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307569} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3417787-0b37-54ba-b621-e6d55ac43b3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306971} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c20d515-1f48-5aec-946c-716105bcbbf0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307810} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfed4f33-2d1f-51a1-a259-d0e2ac8c0f8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307224} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6a5f5a6-0b5f-5445-b33d-5f25bda05525" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308251} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "057dc0c1-9b91-5408-bfb2-87575fdd4609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305200} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8d91ade-2020-5dea-8c9b-3e7b3560fbbb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308313}] :question/id #uuid "64533ce4-1ae9-513d-ba89-484c2cf3a62c" :question/math-academy-id "q-334382" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{0} & 5{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -5{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=5\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-5\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((5\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(5\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(5\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+5\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t &=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308611 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b642857-d5c7-5354-9582-e84b796c8d0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305568} :answer-field/id #uuid "191d5551-a712-5140-91a3-ad273a6ad519" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307600} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfdf9ccd-6d68-52b8-90d2-de98adb98891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306941} :answer-field/id #uuid "69784144-c83c-5567-a773-771397a8e2ee" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307859}] :question/id #uuid "ff10c64d-19c8-5825-958b-92dcd06d6e53" :question/math-academy-id "q-334387" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | ${e}^{3t}-{e}^{-3t}$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | ${e}^{3t}-{e}^{-3t}$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{0} & 3{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-3t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=3t,\n$$\n\nboth of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-3t) &={e}^{-3t} \\\\ r(3t) &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{-3t} \\\\ 3t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtracting the second equation from the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-6t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-3t}-{e}^{3t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{6t}({e}^{-3t}-{e}^{3t}).\n$$\n\n- Adding the first and the second equations, we get\n\n$$\n2{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-3t}+{e}^{3t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-3t}+{e}^{3t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-3t}+{e}^{3t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}) \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t & =3\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{6t}({e}^{-3t}-{e}^{3t}))t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{3t}-{e}^{-3t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{3t}-{e}^{-3t} \\\\ {e}^{3t}-{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308634 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c339771-09ba-5022-9518-b108d54d7a85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305572} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dd870b2-a7c5-5395-803e-55ce4d4f4943" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307713} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a803fbc-355e-5705-83ad-dd81e32fcabc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305395} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f6b70cd-fe87-553d-9371-7a3f6e38337f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbc416a2-fcf3-5f9c-b6c8-072133cbba6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307041} :answer-field/id #uuid "78b8505f-4ff7-51cd-8b58-a89db40093f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307902} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f7fee4a-c580-56e8-ad35-f8a8f1d5812e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306213} :answer-field/id #uuid "f547f3a4-4a17-530c-9994-4e346ffc2d43" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308298}] :question/id #uuid "691520cf-4380-50be-8b5c-ac8a181c7472" :question/math-academy-id "q-334499" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & {\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 0 & 5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=5t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(5t) &={e}^{5t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(5t) &={e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{5t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{5t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n5t{e}^{5t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{5t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{5t}(1-5t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =5{e}^{5t}t+{e}^{5t}(1-5t) \\\\  & ={e}^{5t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & ={e}^{5t}t \\\\  & =t{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365659 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e09b9bd8-e653-5eb4-99a5-e24ca1275327" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365661} {:answer/id #uuid "06aa85f1-3426-574e-99c1-322400e91930" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497814} :answer-field/id #uuid "4302394f-a0de-5281-a556-4c43f2010e3e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365660} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "809ccb92-46bf-593f-aa3e-fab259413c63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365663} {:answer/id #uuid "4148c3f6-7cd3-5b8a-8b0b-2b61c22f4d78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497945} :answer-field/id #uuid "3baf4fff-2224-5b2e-97a5-8950130f9bc3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17f33320-09c2-5afb-8ad2-f98194eb8e4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365665} {:answer/id #uuid "0d0d2d29-ff61-5f5f-b6b0-49c8e2ecf0ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497827} :answer-field/id #uuid "17ad3991-2ac6-5ad3-a913-929c3b64178c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac97a07e-cd49-5c84-a334-f6d1792e26ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365667} {:answer/id #uuid "873e1c15-5d9d-58fe-a62d-ab1be804a1ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(6t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498111} :answer-field/id #uuid "918694ef-b209-599f-9859-2c7968e720c9" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365666}] :question/id #uuid "511649c4-cd9c-5496-8df1-bb8892a20547" :question/math-academy-id "q-334386" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{0} & -6{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=6\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-6\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((6\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(6\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(6\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+6\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t &=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{6t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{6t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365668 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cd42562-09cd-51eb-b4a2-b584bedeb569" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365670} {:answer/id #uuid "9e6ed429-cb7b-5097-aa61-71d601e00811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}+e^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}+e^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442520} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0c533ef-5493-5cd1-a424-830212f48ffc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e04a12ae-abe9-59a0-b308-9184898a8572" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365672} {:answer/id #uuid "90a5ac54-ed2a-5377-933c-378e5c24686e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}+e^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}+e^{-5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442516} :answer-field/id #uuid "df0b6879-e091-50fa-802c-bc06c1af37d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365671}] :question/id #uuid "162963ac-9899-549d-9b3f-b09605170db6" :question/math-academy-id "q-334389" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">${e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">${e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{0} & 5{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-5t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=5t,\n$$\n\neach of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-5t) &={e}^{-5t} \\\\ r(5t) &={e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{-5t} \\\\ 5t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtracting the second equation from the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-10t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-5t}-{e}^{5t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{10t}({e}^{-5t}-{e}^{5t}).\n$$\n\n- Adding the first and the second equations, we get\n\n$$\n2{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-5t}+{e}^{5t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-5t}+{e}^{5t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-5t}+{e}^{5t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t}) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & =5\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{10t}({e}^{-5t}-{e}^{5t}))t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t} & {e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t} \\\\ {e}^{5t}-{e}^{-5t} & {e}^{5t}+{e}^{-5t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365673 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5728e179-6831-5401-a928-e641db0a06b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365675} :answer-field/id #uuid "afbc2e57-8b1b-5ce4-9b27-cb6cab8bfe1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365674} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "979acb26-7ddd-5b55-9211-9925729aa071" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365677} :answer-field/id #uuid "43739f8d-9cc2-5a3f-8f44-3fd681edf8db" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365676} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8029db2d-8bde-50dd-9836-f39ca854a3bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365679} :answer-field/id #uuid "faaddf78-a1db-5496-a708-d82d0e79d47b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365678} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6356927b-4df6-547a-97be-5637f834898e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365681} :answer-field/id #uuid "c911bdd1-5a68-53a2-90c8-77d2d0783bc8" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365680}] :question/id #uuid "93c5b9c1-d3c4-52c5-af95-03ae43585aaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-334497" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & {\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 0 & -4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-4t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-4t) &={e}^{-4t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(-4t) &={e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{-4t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-4t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-4t{e}^{-4t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-4t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-4t}(1+4t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-4{e}^{-4t}t+{e}^{-4t}(1+4t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-4t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & ={e}^{-4t}t \\\\  & =t{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-4t} & t{e}^{-4t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-4t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442558 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447904f5-55a6-51ca-8b1d-4ad7c937739c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442503} :answer-field/id #uuid "17a3fa21-8b4b-539e-b4a9-7b74df9dfc26" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442539} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "966ff2c0-480f-5877-9989-0745484cb033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442517} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a55abe9-c911-599b-b2a8-84db01e3afe2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bde2eae0-1495-58c1-8985-d89c236173c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442526} :answer-field/id #uuid "a293f925-01c4-58f6-9d3b-c977e87aacb0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442550} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df8888c-7ce2-54cf-89a5-a57b8363008d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442486} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa9dd6f0-1904-5376-ac44-6fbcd00dad87" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442555}] :question/id #uuid "9ce1dad2-2fca-5e8c-94e6-f02fef65fbf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-334378" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{0} & 3{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -3{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-3\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((3\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(3\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(3\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+3\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t &=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442559 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64a42564-d378-5079-b530-a07bf0b2b025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442512} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b38ef76-8e2e-55bc-a30d-26d2bb7b9989" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a7f68b9-b84b-550d-8d8e-f599f80550fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442514} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ac308e4-863c-58ff-b1ad-02a8ca98b2f4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442544} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11f4854c-8ae9-549a-b2bb-c9073cef5ff2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442488} :answer-field/id #uuid "6500511e-9f0a-5ef7-9462-e2cebae0ac35" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e574707-9ebd-551d-a80e-32bc19c039cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442495} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d982dfa-f791-5977-9e71-767b13c5022b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442547}] :question/id #uuid "a456bad8-fb03-5da0-aae9-4b577c9cb688" :question/math-academy-id "q-334460" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=t\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=3t\n$$\n\neach of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(t) &={e}^{t} \\\\ r(3t) &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{t} \\\\ 3t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtract the first equation from the second one, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{{e}^{3t}-{e}^{t}}{2t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{3{e}^{t}-{e}^{3t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the diagonal entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{{e}^{3t}-{e}^{t}}{2t}\\cdot t+\\frac{3{e}^{t}-{e}^{3t}}{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{t} \\\\ 3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =3\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3t}-{e}^{t}}{2t}\\cdot t+\\frac{3{e}^{t}-{e}^{3t}}{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afec3c4b-9a72-5853-9cc0-0f4f9ba6a7ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "te^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "te^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442523} :answer-field/id #uuid "335beb98-a9f9-5f49-b0ce-c12df9395ecb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442542} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "571ee1e9-f789-58d1-979f-dadab4a9282e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442508} :answer-field/id #uuid "608539f1-56a3-549b-9b86-eeadf8729d50" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442545} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f915cb8f-1503-5790-a5be-ea9e1669ff66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442534} :answer-field/id #uuid "adc78c25-850b-52fa-9f2b-9ea555ee6ffa" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442551} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a869c1f-ede5-5da6-a338-863911576984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442509} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3a781cc-504f-5f42-9f24-00ce26484a8c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442552}] :question/id #uuid "dc97c5df-528b-5640-b7e6-250d27836f61" :question/math-academy-id "q-334495" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & {\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 0 & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The only eigenvalue of $At$ is \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-t\n$$\n\nof multiplicity two. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-t) &={e}^{-t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\lambda }r(-t) &={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{-t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- From the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-t{e}^{-t}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-t}(1+t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-{e}^{-t}t+{e}^{-t}(1+t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t & ={e}^{-t}t \\\\  & =t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498520 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dae93f70-eae4-559e-a461-fdfe0abd280a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{7t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{7t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498287} :answer-field/id #uuid "3daf4d3b-396f-535d-ab9e-524aea10fa43" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498387} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a35fdcb-73b8-57ed-b501-fbab000af654" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498117} :answer-field/id #uuid "766ab29d-e5ba-5a2d-8e7a-62126c5689d2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498415} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef4cb3a8-c477-5885-9483-f1d0949fce53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498323} :answer-field/id #uuid "913d9aeb-35ba-5403-99b5-0421203894a3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498431} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34c83096-dcf8-5094-a182-51ebd39feed2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497916} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3ef4a65-1363-5281-b2e0-253a6eed11ad" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498448}] :question/id #uuid "3f77715c-0903-5f4b-a449-6816c6d9bb06" :question/math-academy-id "q-334465" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=4t\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=7t\n$$\n\neach of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}r(4t) &={e}^{4t} \\\\ r(7t) &={e}^{7t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{4t} \\\\ 7t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{7t}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtract the first equation from the second one, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{{e}^{7t}-{e}^{4t}}{3t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n4t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{4t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{7{e}^{4t}-4{e}^{7t}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the diagonal entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =4\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{7t}-{e}^{4t}}{3t}\\cdot t+\\frac{7{e}^{4t}-4{e}^{7t}}{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{4t} \\\\ 7{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =7\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{7t}-{e}^{4t}}{3t}\\cdot t+\\frac{7{e}^{4t}-4{e}^{7t}}{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{7t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{7t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a54e01d-d3da-520d-a71e-fb2b3d3a8bd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{6t}+e^{-6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{6t}+e^{-6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533275} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ec158fd-889b-5066-b795-fdf52e06926c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533801} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f40c120d-2ef8-574c-b604-70f11f9600d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{6t}+e^{-6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{6t}+e^{-6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533740} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ac691a2-04d5-52ef-bc49-8d3327cd84e3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533851}] :question/id #uuid "f69ba2b0-76ef-5087-a5bf-906e0adf24a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-334388" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">${e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">${e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr></tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & 6{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-6t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=6t,\n$$\n\neach of multiplicity one. Thus, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-6t)={e}^{-6t} \\\\ r(6t)={e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-6t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-6t} \\\\ 6t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{6t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtracting the second equation from the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-12t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-6t}-{e}^{6t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{12t}({e}^{-6t}-{e}^{6t}).\n$$\n\n- Adding the first and the second equations, we get\n\n$$\n2{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-6t}+{e}^{6t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-6t}+{e}^{6t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-6t}+{e}^{6t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{6t}+{e}^{-6t}) \\\\ 6{\\alpha }_{1}t & =6\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{12t}({e}^{-6t}-{e}^{6t}))t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{6t}+{e}^{-6t} & {e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t} \\\\ {e}^{6t}-{e}^{-6t} & {e}^{6t}+{e}^{-6t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aa1a93d-75a0-5e01-ae23-5b0f8e1ac112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557956} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ae25ef7-c29f-5097-8973-b2adfaba1611" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558377} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37b1d3e9-bd96-5587-a427-f6db2fe1f661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557980} :answer-field/id #uuid "7820253f-f186-5cf9-9944-b249ef50c9a8" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558416} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a08282a0-0997-5c3f-ac2d-158a5280db4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558184} :answer-field/id #uuid "bccb1e87-298a-5c8e-ae6e-cd3c1dfaaf2b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558449} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9a7c02c-3d69-5ee9-b2d1-6e74980ea60e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558337} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc546b2a-f18f-5a02-9cc9-a4dfb2de1de2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558455}] :question/id #uuid "4c0f5df5-2d8b-5cef-a048-d87044456178" :question/math-academy-id "q-334464" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"40px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-t\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2t\n$$\n\neach of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}r(-t)={e}^{-t} \\\\ r(2t)={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-t} \\\\ 2t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtract the first equation from the second one, we get\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{{e}^{2t}-{e}^{-t}}{3t}.\n$$\n\n- Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{-t}}{3}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the diagonal entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-\\frac{{e}^{2t}-{e}^{-t}}{3t}\\cdot t+\\frac{{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{-t}}{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{-t} \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =2\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2t}-{e}^{-t}}{3t}\\cdot t+\\frac{{e}^{2t}+2{e}^{-t}}{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558572 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aec3636-0b05-53aa-b49f-bb68ba34e051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557927} :answer-field/id #uuid "46deef4f-e56b-5e36-8314-39c65e6b0ff6" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f82863e-1510-5b78-bcdf-021a61eb750f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value 